        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0664" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg564"/>

                <head>No. 435.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Heap
                        to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 14, 1884</date>.
                        (Received June 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 388.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit a copy and
                    translation of a note from the Sublime Porte, received recently at the legation,
                    which I think may be accepted as an ultimatum respecting the case of Dr. Pflaum.
                    Further action on our part, if any is taken, now rests with the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. H. HEAP.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d435-a1.xml" xpointer="d435-a1"/>
            </div>
